 "narrative": [
  "To be admitted to full major status, students must fulfill the pre-biology course and grade-point average requirements as described in the General Catalog. At minimum, they must complete twelve eleven designated courses from the Preparation for the Major with a 2.0 or higher UC grade-point average. Note: Hyphens indicate that an entire sequence or combination must be completed as shown to fulfill an area requirement. A single course can satisfy only one requirement. Grades earned must meet the grade prerequisites for the full major.",
  "MAJOR REGULATIONSPREREQUISITES Check the General Catalog for the prerequisites to all listed courses.\nP/NP GRADING OPTION Not allowed for major courses (prep or UD), including courses applied to the major from other departments, except up to 8 units of courses that do not allow letter grades.\nSUBSTITUTIONS In the major requirements permissible only by petition to the department chair and dean.\nG.P.A. REQUIREMENTS At least 2.0 overall UC average in all upper-division major courses and all courses (Prep and UD) for the major.\nDOUBLE MAJORS With the approval of each department chairperson, up to a total of 8 units may be applied simultaneously to both UD majors."
 ],
